openmamba           GNU/Linux                                                                                                                                 is            a                        distribution     for               personal          computers     that           can              be            used           on                   notebooks,     desktops,     servers        and              Raspberry      Pi             computers.    It            works               as            an                  installable        live                 DVD/USB        images,          offering      one           of                two              desktop       environments:  KDE             Plasma           or           LXQt.         The           distribution  uses                 RPM            packages         managed           through        the            DNF                package        manager.          Software        can             also          be               fetched        and            installed       from           Flatpak           repositories.    openmamba                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
